{% set local_problem %}
<p>Hampton Cove homes are built to high standards — but even quality construction can't fully protect against Alabama's humidity. When builder-grade gutters leak or overflow (which they often do), water saturates the fascia boards behind them. Combined with our hot, humid summers, rot develops over time.</p>

<p>The tricky part is that rot often hides behind paint that looks perfectly fine from the ground. Homeowners have no idea there's a problem until gutters start pulling away from the house or we probe the wood during a gutter estimate and find it soft.</p>

<p>For Hampton Cove homes, we use quality materials that match the neighborhood's standards — composite or treated lumber that resists moisture and lasts longer than standard fascia boards.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our repair process includes: thorough assessment of damage extent (rot often spreads beyond what's visible); removal of damaged sections back to solid wood; treatment of adjacent areas to prevent spread; installation of new fascia using moisture-resistant materials; and preparation for gutter installation.</p>

<p>We match existing trim profiles and can prime or paint to match your home's colors.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We handle fascia repair in-house, using quality materials appropriate for Hampton Cove homes. One crew, one job, one company standing behind everything.</p>

<p>We understand that quality matters here — both in materials and workmanship.</p>
{% endset %}

